<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Golf - Mixed fortunes for Spanish Ryder Cup hopes.</title>
<headline>Golf - Mixed fortunes for Spanish Ryder Cup hopes.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE  1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spaniard Miguel Martin's hopes of a Ryder Cup debut plummeted on Wednesday when he learned he will be out of golf for a minimum six weeks after an operation on his wrist.</p>
<p>Martin, currently eighth in the Ryder Cup points table, looks certain to drop out of the top 10 who gain automatic selection on the team to face the U.S. before the cut-off date of August 31</p>
<p>He could be overtaken in this week's Czech Open by Costantino Rocca of Italy (ninth in the table), Spaniard Ignacio Garrido (10th), and Ireland's Padraig Harrington (11th).</p>
</text>
